    "description": {
      "gm": "",
      "value": "<p class=\"MsoNormal\"><strong>Requirements</strong> You have a creature grabbed or restrained.</p><p><strong>Frequency</strong> Once per round</p><hr><p class=\"MsoNormal\"><span style=\"mso-bidi-font-size:12.0pt;mso-bidi-font-family:Calibri;mso-bidi-theme-font:minor-latin;mso-bidi-font-weight:bold\">As you have someone gripped by your tail or by your teeth, you can clamp down to give them a firm squeeze. The creature must make a basic Fortitude save against your class DC or take @Damage[3d6[bludgeoning]]{bludgeoning damage}. You increase the number of damage die by 1 if your unarmed attack benefits from a Greater Striking rune, or 2 if it benefits from a Major striking rune. This DC benefits from any bonuses you have to your Athletics checks or DCs.</span></p>"
